            <ArticleTitle>Bromocriptine for the management of autonomic dysfunction after severe traumatic brain injury.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>283-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This case report describes a child with severe traumatic brain injury with clinical features of autonomic dysfunction in the immediate post-traumatic period. A history of severe asthma in this child contraindicated the use of beta-blockers, the first line approach, and she was managed with bromocriptine (0.05 mg/kg t.d.s) with good effect.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
